# Ponytail hygiene

- Keep each module to a single responsibility. Split files whose description needs "and".
- Delete unused code, commented-out blocks, and pass-through wrappers in the files you touch.
- Name types and functions with the PRD's domain language.
- Keep I/O at the edges so core logic stays unit-testable.
- Do not reformat or refactor unrelated modules.
- Concurrency control (version, lock, idempotency key) must be visible at the write site.
